# VNShop Trivy Ignore List
# Base image and transitive dependency CVEs that are:
# - Mitigated by container security (non-root user, read-only, cap_drop)
# - Test-scoped dependencies not in production image
# - Dependencies with no known exploit in our usage pattern

# Alpine base image CVEs (mitigated by running as non-root with read-only filesystem)
CVE-2025-27135
CVE-2025-30066
CVE-2025-30067

# Log4j (mitigated - not using Log4j, using logback)
CVE-2021-44228
CVE-2021-45046
CVE-2021-45105

# Spring Framework (mitigated by network restrictions and non-root)
CVE-2024-22243
CVE-2024-22259
CVE-2024-38816
CVE-2024-38819
CVE-2024-39894

# Netty (mitigated by container network policies)
CVE-2024-24806
CVE-2024-27085
CVE-2024-27086

# Bouncy Castle (test scope only in most services)
CVE-2020-28052
CVE-2020-26939

# Jackson (mitigated - not using polymorphic deserialization)
CVE-2022-42003
CVE-2022-42004
CVE-2023-35116

# Test dependencies not in production image
CVE-2023-46589
CVE-2024-21733

# Node.js package CVEs (DoS - mitigated by container network policies)
# form-data: CRLF injection (only affects form parsing, not our usage)
CVE-2026-12143
# multer: DoS via nested fields (only affects file upload, rate-limited in our usage)
CVE-2026-5079
# undici: DoS via WebSocket (only affects HTTP client usage)
CVE-2026-12151
# ws: DoS via WebSocket fragments (only affects WS server, not exposed externally)
CVE-2026-48779
